> Overpowered IMO. Perhaps +enchantment Cha instead of messing with luck?

I think it wouldn't be worth making an artefact just for a Charisma
bonus - the _non-artefact_ Helm of Brilliance has something a lot
better than that. And i was under the impression that the suggested
luck bonus was supposed to be +1 or +2, which is a far cry from
powerful, let alone overpowered. Once you possess a luckstone and have
played around with an altar or friendly unicorn, another _five_ points
of luck wouldn't make a significant difference. Hmmm ... wouldn't this
need to be a special power, too, to prevent an actual luckstone from
over-riding it?

How about if it was worn it'd grant you a magic-cancellation saving
throw against memory loss when being brain-sucked? Wouldn't prevent
intelligence loss and wouldn't help against scrolls of amnesia. Would
make it pretty desirable but not a guaranteed safety device. 

Temporary "resistance" as invocation effect doesn't sound very
attractive to me - and is there any artefact which gives an actual
temporary effect right now? Either (H,M,P,R,T,V,W quest artefacts) the
effect is instantaneous, or (A,B,C quest artefacts) it's effectively
permanent (all the time until it leaves your inventory or until you
#invoke it again to switch it off, which you can elect to never do).

